<article class="prose">
  <p class="eyebrow">Guide</p>
  <h1>Assigning</h1>
  <p class="lede">Assign all of your money to a spending category. This is your spending plan for the month.</p>

  <h2>Ready to Assign</h2>
  <p>Money that has come in and has no category assigned yet is <strong>Ready to Assign</strong>. On the Budget tab it shows as <strong>To Budget</strong>. Record income as an <strong>Inflow</strong> with the category Ready to Assign, and that amount appears here.</p>

  <section class="guide-split">
    <div class="copy">
  <h2>Categories and groups</h2>
  <p>Categories are where money is assigned. Putting money in a category is how you budget for spending. Spending lowers that category’s available balance. Assign enough each month to cover the spending you expect. A negative amount means the category was overspent. Assign more money there to cover it.</p>
  <p>Groups organize related categories, such as Essentials.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>On iPhone, tap the category and edit <strong>Assigned</strong>.</li>
    <li>On Mac, click the category’s <strong>Assigned</strong> amount.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can also move available money from one category to another.</p>
    </div>
